Ladybird picks a tab’s font the way it picks a space’s. In Chrome
157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5, a <pre> line holding
a tab, in a font list whose first face has no U+0009 (Courier New
under unicode-range: U+0020-007E) and whose next is Zapfino, is
as tall as one without a tab: 18px in Chrome and WebKit, 19px in
Firefox, where a line holding U+00A2, which only Zapfino has, is
54px. WebKit’s FontCascade::treatAsSpace() lists the tab among the
characters it treats as spaces.
